      "program": "Chemistry, Georgia State University",
      "program_name": "Chemistry",
      "university": "Georgia State University",
      "comments": "Submitted my application in November before the priority deadline, and paid the application fee. On the day of the priority deadline, they extended the deadline further. They waived the application fee for all applicants who had not submitted their applications and wished to apply later. Due to a system error, my application was not under review, but the portal was showing both under review and awaiting materials status. When I reached out to one of the advisors on May 12, they corrected their error and finally got a rejection letter on 29th May. From these circumstances, I can assume that my application did not get a proper review. Before May, I had reached out to the official email of the College of Arts and Sciences, which was the only communication method for them regarding the application, but I never got any response.",
